# Probabilistic Decision Maker
# Weak stimulus drives two competing populations; mutual inhibition creates winner-take-all dynamics.

Define a network named stochastic_decision with timestep 0.002.
# Network with 1 input, 3 LIF neurons, 4 linear transforms, 1 output.
# flow: input → stimulus → choice_A → output
#        stimulus → choice_B
#        (mutual inhibition: choice_A ⇄ choice_B)

# Layers:
Define an input port named input with shape (10,).
Define a LIF neuron named stimulus with time constant 0.02, resistance 1.0, leak voltage 0.0, and firing threshold 1.0.
Define a linear transformation named w_stimulus_choice_A with weight matrix shape (40, 10) annotated with metadata weight_init equal to "xavier" annotated with metadata seed equal to 42.
Define a linear transformation named w_stimulus_choice_B with weight matrix shape (40, 10) annotated with metadata weight_init equal to "xavier" annotated with metadata seed equal to 43.
Define a LIF neuron named choice_A with time constant 0.02, resistance 1.0, leak voltage 0.0, and firing threshold 0.75.
Define a linear transformation named w_choice_A_choice_B with weight matrix shape (40, 40).
# inhibitory connection (weights will be negative) — zero-initialised intentionally
Define a LIF neuron named choice_B with time constant 0.02, resistance 1.0, leak voltage 0.0, and firing threshold 0.75.
Define a linear transformation named w_choice_B_choice_A with weight matrix shape (40, 40).
# inhibitory connection (weights will be negative) — zero-initialised intentionally
Define an output port named output with shape (40,).

# Connections:
input connects to stimulus.
stimulus connects to w_stimulus_choice_A.
w_stimulus_choice_A connects to choice_A.
stimulus connects to w_stimulus_choice_B.
w_stimulus_choice_B connects to choice_B.
choice_A connects to output.

# recurrent: choice_A ↺ choice_B
choice_A connects to w_choice_A_choice_B.
w_choice_A_choice_B connects to choice_B.
choice_B connects to w_choice_B_choice_A.
w_choice_B_choice_A connects to choice_A.

# Note: background noise, homeostasis (15 Hz target), STP, and neuromodulation are dropped.
# Future extension: encode as metadata on population nodes.
